inst/element-plus/ contains unmodified copies of Element Plus 2.14.7
(dist/index.full.min.js, its 67 locales under dist/locale/, and
theme-chalk's index.css, display.css and dark/css-vars.css) and of
@element-plus/icons-vue 2.3.2 (dist/index.iife.min.js), bundled so the
package works without fetching anything at runtime. Eleven locales are
files; the other 56 are packed, unmodified, in dist/locale/more.tar.gz.
Sources: https://github.com/element-plus/element-plus and
https://github.com/element-plus/element-plus-icons. Both are copyright the Element Plus team and
released under the MIT licence; see inst/element-plus/LICENSE and
inst/element-plus/icons-vue.LICENSE.

inst/vue3/ contains Vue 3.5.43, copyright Yuxi (Evan) You and Vue
contributors and released under the MIT licence; see inst/vue3/LICENSE.
Source: https://github.com/vuejs/core.
vue.global.prod.js is an unmodified copy of dist/vue.global.prod.js.
The development build, dist/vue.global.js, is in the package's sources
(minified with terser 5: `terser vue.global.js --compress --mangle
--comments '/^!|@license|vue v/'`; its code, warnings included, otherwise
unchanged) but not in the package built for CRAN, which loads it from the
unpkg CDN when asked for it.

inst/dayjs/locale/ contains unmodified copies of Day.js 1.11.20's locale
files (locale/*.js) for the languages Element Plus has a locale for: Day.js
itself is part of Element Plus's build, whose date components read their
locale from it. Ten are files; the other 51 are packed, unmodified, in
inst/dayjs/locale/more.tar.gz. Day.js is copyright iamkun and released
under the MIT licence; see inst/dayjs/LICENSE.
Source: https://github.com/iamkun/dayjs.
